{
  "id": "maximum-subarray",
  "title": "Maximum Subarray",
  "contract": "Return the maximum sum of a nonempty contiguous subarray. Input is nonempty; sums use long.",
  "signature": "long solve(int[] a)",
  "brute": "long best=Long.MIN_VALUE;\nfor(int i=0;i<a.length;i++) { long sum=0; for(int j=i;j<a.length;j++) {\n  sum+=a[j];best=Math.max(best,sum);emit(\"Extend a candidate interval\", \"range\",new int[]{i,j},\"sum\",sum,\"best\",best);\n}}\nreturn best;",
  "optimal": "long ending=a[0],best=a[0];emit(\"Initialize a nonempty subarray\", \"ending\",ending,\"best\",best);\nfor(int i=1;i<a.length;i++) {\n  ending=Math.max(a[i],ending+a[i]);best=Math.max(best,ending);\n  emit(\"Restart here or extend the previous best ending here\", \"index\",i,\"ending\",ending,\"best\",best);\n}\nreturn best;",
  "reasoning": [
    "Enumerate starts and incrementally extend each end; a third summation loop is unnecessary.",
    "Any best subarray ending at i either begins at i or extends the best subarray ending at i−1.",
    "Track a separate global maximum. Initializing to zero would incorrectly choose an empty interval for all-negative input."
  ],
  "complexity": [
    "O(n²), O(1)",
    "O(n), O(1)"
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "label": "Mixed",
      "args": "new int[]{-2,1,-3,4,-1,2,1,-5,4}",
      "expected": "6"
    },
    {
      "label": "Negative",
      "args": "new int[]{-4,-2,-8}",
      "expected": "-2"
    }
  ],
